(4) VERDICTS
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
[V1] PASS
    THE POOLED LINE ACROSS 10^2.6-10^14.4: OLS slope b = 0.988 +- 0.020 on N = 248 objects (the comprehensive Nu = 1 test: (b-1)/se = -0.57), rms about the identity line 0.221 dex; the CORE population (GC+bright dSph+HI+SPARC, the on-line channels) gives b = 0.987 +- 0.024, rms 0.191 dex. The pooled rms is set by the two REGISTERED end departures (UFD +0.40, clusters +0.27/+0.55 dex), not by slope curvature.
[V2] PASS
    OVERLAP-CHANNEL CONSISTENCY at 10^6.25-10^7.51 M_sun: the dispersion channel (dSphs: median |r| 0.114, median r -0.114) and the rotation channel (HI dwarfs: median |r| 0.056, median r +0.012) observe the SAME masses and land on the SAME line within ~0.07 dex combined -- v_flat = (G M_b a0)^(1/4) and sigma = v/sqrt(2) are one line at fixed mass, not two calibrations.
[V3] PASS
    HONEST: the law is ONE line across ~12 decades -- the comprehensive Nu = 1 test at the pooled level gives b = 0.988 +- 0.020 on N = 248 objects ((b-1)/se = -0.57) and the macro-channel fit b = 0.976 +- 0.081; the wide-dynamic-range channels TRACE the line internally (HI 0.92+-0.15, SPARC 1.03+-0.09, clusters 0.85+-0.13), while the narrow dispersion windows CROSS it (bright dSph sigma plateau, Nu = 0.46; GC virial locus, Nu = 2.36) at zero points +0.05/+0.06 -- with THREE quantified exceptions: (1) the UFD dispersion departure, +0.40 dex median over 20 objects (obs sigma ~2.5x pred; residual slope +0.16 +- 0.02 per dex -- the low-end split); (2) the cluster normalization gap, T_obs/T_pred = 3.57x (+0.55 dex in T, +0.27 dex in sigma_dyn,3D), tight at 0.05-dex scatter -- parallel, offset; the registered free-dust normalization stays an input; (3) the GC crossing at M_cross = 1.23e5 M_sun, r_M/r_h = 3.39 = eta/2. THE NUMBER: pooled rms 0.221 dex over N = 248 objects (rms about the identity line); the TRIO that both traces and calibrates the line (bright dSph + HI + SPARC) holds it to 0.135 dex -- the 10-decade line is ONE slope-1 line at ~0.15-dex precision, with two known amplitude departures at its ends (UFD, clusters), not a slope artifact and not a set of per-mass calibrations.

